+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
| Running ${PKGSTEM} on OpenBSD
+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Resource limits
===============

The ad blocker uses large content filter lists which WebKit compiles inside
the epiphany process on first start, and whenever the lists are updated.
With the default lists this requires a lot of memory; if the data size limit is
reached, epiphany crashes with "Illegal instruction" (WebKit's allocator
aborting on out of memory).

Increase your datasize limit using `ulimit -Sd' (you can make this permanent in
login.conf(5).

Or disable the ad blocker entirely:
    $ gsettings set org.gnome.Epiphany.web:/org/gnome/epiphany/web/ enable-adblock false
